  "mathematical_scope": [
    "The same actual rootInverseCoordinate(rootFlowParameterUnscale Theta delta)(n01RootLabel ...) supplies both genuine Seeley extensions. No new chart, flow, label, component, host or state is selected.",
    "The even output is its angular displacement, including order zero. The odd output is the genuine smooth negative-odd coefficient, not the totalized divided quotient at the boundary.",
    "A fixed finite prefix through n+1 of the same actual inverse-coordinate displacement gives M. Its positive source jets are at most M+1<=2M because the angular projection has all positive jet norms at most one.",
    "The two independently reviewed local linear operator estimates produce CE*M and CO*2M. The common coefficient precedes source, extension, angle and M.",
    "The actual normalized root flow equations and the original label derive global smoothness and pi-equivariance needed by the fixed extensions; these are not added terminal assumptions.",
    "All material coefficients precede state, component, host, profile factor, strip radius, parameter scale, selected flow and angle. The same low order is retained; the common loss is inputLoss+1. High grading occurs only once.",
    "The material scale is the same C0 times E0(sample j), with its proven floor at one. Neither the arbitrary localization radius R nor normalization delta is charged."
  ],
  "scope_caveat": "Raw same-component optical lower and actual host containment are still explicit upstream conditions, and actual OrdinaryFlowJacobianBounds is explicit. The current Through03 contract does not expose the raw optical lower. Nonlinear radial/height powers, positive midpoint conversion, SmoothDirections and the final N04c bounds are not claimed.",
